    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0186" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/11–749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Thailand</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stanton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-07T13:00:00+07:00">November 7, 1949—1
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 7—11:03 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>951 Foreign Minister<anchor n="94" xml:id="d188-f1"/> informs me telegram
                    received from Prince Wan<anchor n="95" xml:id="d188-f2"/> reporting Dept asked
                    him ascertain view Thailand Govt re recognition Chinese Communist government.
                    Pote said, frankly speaking, Government hoped avoid recognition long as
                    possible. I enquired precisely what he meant by this term. He replied Government
                    hoped delay establishment diplomatic relations until Chinese Communist
                    government seated in UN and implied that early recognition by Britain or other
                    countries would probably not affect Government’s present position this matter.
                    He went on to explain establishment diplomatic relations would be grave
                    development for Thailand since it was anticipated Chinese Communist diplomats,
                    consular representatives, would actively endeavor form Chinese minority this
                    country into active pro-Communist unit. Evident from what he said Government
                    rather hopes will be possible avoid exchange diplomatic representatives even in
                    event recognition Chinese Communist govt and that with this in mind formation
                    special Chinese affairs department under Ministry Interior being pushed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d188-f1" n="94" xml:id="d188-f1-content">
                <p>Pote Sarasin.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d188-f2" n="95" xml:id="d188-f2-content">
                <p>Prince Wan Waithayakon, Thai Ambassador in the United States.</p>
            </note>
